<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 2026-07-08</p>

<p>
This Privacy Policy applies to the mobile game <strong>BLOCK RUSH BLAST</strong>
(package name: <code>com.plutogames.blockrush</code>) published by <strong>PlutoGames</strong>.
</p>

<h3>1) Summary</h3>
<ul>
  <li>We do <strong>not</strong> require account creation and we do <strong>not</strong> provide cloud save.</li>
  <li>Game progress is stored <strong>locally on your device</strong>.</li>
  <li>We may use third-party services such as Firebase Analytics, Google Play Billing, and advertising services, which may process limited data.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2) Data we collect</h3>
<p>We may collect limited data to operate, measure, and improve the game:</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>App interactions / usage data</strong> such as app opens, screens viewed, session length, and gameplay events
    for analytics and performance improvements.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Device & app identifiers</strong> such as an app-instance / installation identifier used by analytics.
    If ads are enabled, we or our ad partners may also use advertising identifiers such as the Android Advertising ID
    and/or App Set ID depending on device settings and SDK configuration.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Diagnostics</strong> such as performance information and crash-related data if diagnostic or crash reporting is enabled.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>In-app purchase information</strong> such as product ID and purchase status to deliver purchased items and restore purchases,
    if in-app purchases are available in the game. Payment details are handled by Google Play and are not received by us.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>3) Local game data (no account / no cloud save)</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Progress is stored locally</strong> on your device, for example your level progress, coins, game settings, and similar gameplay data.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you uninstall the game, local data stored on the device is typically removed with the app.
    We do not offer account-based syncing or cloud backup within the game.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>4) How we use data</h3>
<ul>
  <li>To measure retention, session length, gameplay behavior, and improve performance and user experience.</li>
  <li>To show ads and help prevent fraud or abuse related to ads, if ads are enabled.</li>
  <li>To process and validate in-app purchases and deliver purchased content, if purchases are available.</li>
  <li>To diagnose crashes, bugs, and performance issues if diagnostic tools are enabled.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5) Third-party services</h3>
<p>We may use third-party services that collect and process data according to their own policies:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Google Firebase / Google Analytics</strong> for analytics and measurement</li>
  <li><strong>Google Play Billing</strong> for in-app purchases, if purchases are available</li>
  <li><strong>Google AdMob / Google Mobile Ads SDK</strong> for advertisements, if ads are enabled</li>
  <li><strong>AppLovin MAX</strong> for advertisements and ad mediation, if enabled</li>
</ul>

<h3>6) Data sharing</h3>
<p>
We do not sell personal data.
Data may be processed and/or shared with the service providers listed above only to provide analytics, advertising,
purchase functionality, fraud prevention, diagnostics, and app performance features.
</p>

<h3>7) Security</h3>
<p>
We do not operate our own user account servers for this game.
We rely on reputable third-party providers and use reasonable measures to protect data.
For example, data transmission is handled using secure connections where applicable, and access to tools such as Firebase,
Google Play services, AdMob, or AppLovin is limited to authorized use for operating the game.
</p>

<h3>8) Data retention and deletion</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    We retain data only as long as necessary to operate and improve the game, comply with legal obligations,
    prevent fraud or abuse, and resolve disputes. Retention periods may vary depending on the provider settings.
  </li>
  <li>
    You can reset or limit the Android Advertising ID in your device settings. This may affect personalized ads.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you contact us, we can provide guidance on deletion options available through our providers,
    for example deleting or resetting identifiers used by analytics services where available.
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>9) Your choices</h3>
<ul>
  <li>You can limit ad personalization and reset your Advertising ID via Android or Google settings.</li>
  <li>You can contact us for privacy and data questions.</li>
  <li>You can uninstall the game to remove locally stored game data from your device, subject to your device and platform behavior.</li>
</ul>

<h3>10) Children’s privacy</h3>
<p>
We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
If you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps.
</p>

<h3>11) Changes to this policy</h3>
<p>
We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated “Last updated” date.
</p>

